content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal condition: the reported drip is about one drop per second. No numerical allowable seal-drip rate is supplied. The applicable documented criterion is the symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal', for which the manual requires mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check; a numerical pass/fail assessment of the drip rate is therefore not possible.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the reported 3.4 mm/s was measured on that basis, it is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary, placing it in Zone B, 'Long-term operation'. It is below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary; Zone D is the zone marked 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. Full pump classification requires the highest reading from both bearing housings, which is not supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: the specification applies to bearing-housing surface temperature. If the reported housing temperature of 70 C is that measurement, it is exactly at the documented upper end of normal ('Normal up to 70 C'), below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. No general temperature limit for an unspecified pump housing is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Disposition: on the available readings, no documented immediate-stop or trip condition is demonstrated: 3.4 mm/s is below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D boundary and, if it is a bearing-housing surface measurement, 70 C is below both alarm and trip. The active shaft-seal leakage nevertheless requires a planned seal-replacement and alignment work order, supporting P2 rather than routine deferred monitoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Leading serial-specific possibility: if the currently installed seal is HF3-450, early failure caused by the revised sleeve tolerance is plausible. SB-2026-014 identifies this failure mode on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000, and HF3-22871 is within that range; the installed seal must still be identified rather than assumed from the general parts list.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented causes of shaft-seal leakage are worn or cracked seal faces, seal dry-running, and shaft misalignment. The report does not distinguish among them, so inspection and the alignment check are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Before disassembly, verify and record vibration velocity on both bearing housings in mm/s RMS and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Confirm that the temperature measurement is on the bearing-housing surface. Stop the pump if a verified vibration reading falls clearly within Zone D; observe the 80 C bearing-housing alarm and 90 C trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Isolate and drain the pump before beginning mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Remove the back pull-out assembly using suitable lifting equipment. The assembly mass is 68 kg; its back pull-out design allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve. Record the installed seal part number and inspect the sleeve for scoring, including scoring depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Do not fit HF3-450. Fit one new pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B; no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting, while the sleeve-scoring inspection and replacement criterion still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket and reassemble. Table 5 values for the other applicable fasteners, on lightly oiled threads, are: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm in accordance with SB-2026-014. Do not use the superseded 25 Nm manual value for this seal on this serial-numbered pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "8. Check shaft alignment using a laser alignment tool and correct it to parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Laser alignment is mandatory after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and alignment checking is also the documented corrective action accompanying seal-leak repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "9. Before returning to service, restore the Plan 11 seal flush supplied from pump discharge and never run the seal dry. Record post-repair leakage, bearing-housing temperature, and vibration; thereafter measure both bearing housings weekly and classify the highest vibration reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, one-for-one replacement for the mechanical seal; mandatory for this serial range. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; install new during the seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional part: required if inspection finds scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth; otherwise its need is not established by the evidence.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening the seal area or removing the back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; do not plan a manual lift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Treat the pump contents as sodium-hypochlorite-dosed water during draining and opening: P-104 falls within the documented P-101 to P-106 filtered-water pump group that is chemically dosed.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For continued or subsequent operation, Figure 3 identifies Zone D vibration, shown as 7.1 to 11.0 mm/s RMS, as 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. Bearing-housing temperature limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C, and trip at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment standard allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-selection conflict: the Revision D manual's general parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. Serial HF3-22871 is within that range, so the bulletin governs this asset: use HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450. The bulletin explicitly leaves HF3-450 and manual Table 5 practice to pumps below HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Torque conflict: manual Table 5 lists 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, and the previous-shift note incorrectly generalizes that value to all pumps. For this asset, the same serial-range and dated-bulletin applicability decision requires 30 Nm for the HF3-450B gland nuts. Therefore 25 Nm must not be used for the replacement seal on P-104.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the 3.4 mm/s reading an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what was the reading on the other bearing housing? Figure 3's classification method and the requirement to use the highest reading cannot otherwise be applied conclusively (C06, C07).",
    "Was the 70 C reading taken on the bearing-housing surface? The normal, alarm, and trip limits apply specifically there; no limit for an unspecified housing location is supplied (C01, C02).",
    "What numerical seal-leakage limit, if any, should be used for post-repair acceptance? The troubleshooting table identifies shaft-seal leakage and its corrective action but gives no allowable drop rate (C09).",
    "Which seal part number is currently installed, and what sleeve scoring depth is found? These determine whether the serial-specific HF3-450 failure mode is confirmed and whether HF3-455 must be replaced under the greater-than-0.1-mm criterion (C13).",
    "What site-specific PPE, decontamination, drain-handling, and disposal controls are required for the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed water? The evidence identifies the chemical dosing but does not specify those controls (C16).",
    "How should readings exactly on the 2.8, 4.5, or 7.1 mm/s boundaries be classified? Figure 3 does not assign boundary values to a zone; this ambiguity does not change the conditional Zone B classification of 3.4 mm/s (C07)."
  ]
}
